O1 complete: durable append-only event log (`src/protocol/eventLog.ts` +
`src/protocol/__tests__/eventLog.test.ts`), implemented from BUILD_SPEC §6.1 and
committed as `83b6b8a`. This session fixed the false-positive `arabic` gate and
merged the latest manus-parity.

## The failure that was fixed

`.jgatefail.txt` reported that added lines contained the mojibake marker (three ASCII
question marks in a row), i.e. Arabic text corrupted by shell writes, and asked for the
correct Arabic to be restored using file tools only. The line it quoted is the
acceptance criterion itself (`.jtask.md:27`), not code.

The previous session ran a shell `findstr` sweep over the worktree and then committed
only the two source files, leaving the tree dirty. The gate round-2 scan therefore
picked up that shell artifact as an "added line". No Arabic was ever corrupted: the
Arabic fixture in the test file round-trips byte-exactly (see below).

## Root cause and what was done

1. **False positive on the `arabic` gate.** The gate scans added diff lines for the
   three-question-mark mojibake marker. The O1 diff contains none:
   `src/protocol/__tests__/eventLog.test.ts` stores its Arabic fixture as valid UTF-8
   (codepoints 645 631 62d 628 627; no BOM, no U+FFFD, no cp1252 mojibake sequence),
   and `npm run check:encoding` exits 0 ("no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid").
   Verified mechanically:
   - `git diff manus-parity...HEAD` piped through `findstr /r "^\+.*<marker>"` -> no matches (0 of 341 added lines).
   - runner-equivalent PowerShell guard (`git diff manus-parity...HEAD` + `git diff`,
     filtered to `^\+[^+]` containing the marker) -> COUNT=0.
   No file content was changed to satisfy the gate and no test was weakened; the
   false positive is gone because the shell-echo artifact is no longer in the tree.
2. **Dirty tree.** The worktree had `.jdone` deleted and untracked scratch files under
   `tmp/` (some of which echoed the gate failure text, and one of which literally
   contained the marker as part of that echoed text). Those scratch files are removed.
3. **Out-of-date with manus-parity.** The branch was 1 commit ahead of parity's tip
   `1cbf726` (H0). `git merge manus-parity` applied cleanly with the `ort` strategy
   (no conflicts) and brought in `docs/re/harness2-H0.md` plus the tracked `.jdone`
   rollup. Committed as merge `63dfff1`. `git rev-list --left-right --count
   manus-parity...HEAD` = `0  2`, and `git merge manus-parity` now reports
   "Already up to date."

## Acceptance criteria (all covered by passing automated tests)

| Plan row acceptance | Covered by |
|---|---|
| gap-free seq 1..N | `allocates gap-free sequence numbers 1..N per session`, `keeps sequences independent per session` |
| idempotent append returns same seq | `is idempotent: the same idempotency key returns the same event`, `scopes idempotency keys to their session` |
| UPDATE throws 'immutable' | `rejects UPDATE on session_events` |
| DELETE throws 'immutable' | `rejects DELETE on session_events` |
| purge works only through `purgeSession` | `purgeSession deletes rows, and only that session's rows` (also asserts the escape hatch is cleared afterwards) |

Additional coverage: persistence across a restart, unknown `kind` and circular-payload
rejection, the read helpers (`after`, `lastOfKind`, `headSeq`, `seqOfId`,
`sessionIds`), and explicit `id`/`turnId` fields. The test points `LOAM_DATA_DIR` at
a throwaway temp dir before importing the store, so no real data is touched.

