D15 — PR reviewer + bug catcher: DONE

Summary
-------
Adds the `pr_review({repo, number, postComments?, maxFiles?, conventions?})` tool. It
fetches the PR's diff through the D1 `PrProvider` (`pr_diff`, added to the interface and
implemented by `GitHubPrProvider` via `GET /repos/{repo}/pulls/{n}/files?per_page=100` and
by `LocalPrProvider` from a scripted `setPrDiff` seed), reviews each changed file on its
own against the repo conventions (`AGENTS.md` / `CONTRIBUTING.md` when present), and
returns deduplicated findings `{severity: bug|flag|nit, file, line, explanation,
suggested_fix}`. With `postComments` the findings are filed as line review comments through
the same provider.

Implemented end to end:
  - Reviewer:        src/agent/prReview.ts
  - Tool + registry: src/tools/prReviewTools.ts, src/setup/runtime.ts
  - Provider diff:   src/tools/gitPrProvider.ts (PrDiff/PrFileDiff, prDiff on both providers,
                     LocalPrProvider.setPrDiff / setPrDiff helper)
  - Mode allowlist:  src/modes/catalog.ts (`pr_review` in the GIT set)
  - Prompt catalog:  prompts/loam-master.md §6.3 + §8.5, regenerated into
                     src/agent/masterPromptText.ts (snapshot hash refreshed)

Acceptance criteria (AC) met
----------------------------
  - seeded off-by-one bug reported as `bug` at the right file/line
      fixture `src/counter.ts` with `for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++)` on new-file line 7;
      the reviewer parses the hunk headers itself and clamps the model's line into the
      touched range, so the finding lands on `src/counter.ts:7` ->
      src/tools/__tests__/prReview.test.ts ("reports a bug finding at the seeded off-by-one line")
  - duplicates merged (most severe wins, fuller explanation kept, loser's fix merged)
      -> src/tools/__tests__/prReview.test.ts ("merges duplicate findings the model repeats")
  - post-comments goes to LocalProvider only (GitHub posting is exercised through a
    mocked fetch; the tool only ever calls the provider's `addComment`)
      -> src/tools/__tests__/prReview.test.ts ("posts the findings as review comments only when asked")

No network in tests: the diff comes from `LocalPrProvider` seeded with `setPrDiff`, the
model is a fake client returning canned JSON, and the GitHub path is exercised with a
mocked `fetch`.

