## Root cause found during the repair
The conflict was NOT a plain textual conflict. The worktree's git **index was corrupt**
(`error: bad signature 0x00000000` / `fatal: index file corrupt`), and a prior failed merge
had **zeroed out ~21 tracked files on disk** plus deleted `.jdone`.

Repair sequence (all inside the worktree; no forbidden path touched):
1. Renamed the corrupt `index` to `index.corrupt.bak` under
   `C:\Users\khamis\Desktop\manus-local\.git\worktrees\devin-d19\` and rebuilt it with
   `git read-tree HEAD`; `git merge --abort` then succeeded.
2. `git restore` every zeroed tracked file from HEAD (loop.ts, orchestrator.ts, ollama.ts,
   appVerification.ts, contextCompressor.ts, events.ts, independentAcceptance.ts,
   verifier.ts, protocol/events.ts, protocol/types.ts, packages/shared/src/socket.ts,
   packages/web/public/marketplace/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, EventList.tsx, i18n/ar.json,
   i18n/en.json, .jdone). All verified non-zero afterward.
3. Recovered the 7 untracked (parity-only) zeroed files from the `manus-parity` tree via
   `git cat-file blob manus-parity:<path>` (forward slashes required): kvCacheMonitor.ts,
   usageAccounting.ts, cacheUsageAccounting.test.ts, kvCacheMonitor.test.ts,
   cacheUsageEvents.test.ts, CacheUsageRow.tsx, cacheUsageRow.test.tsx.

